# API Development Guidelines

The @10up/block-components library includes API utilities for extending the WordPress Block Editor.

## API Design

- APIs should be simple and intuitive to use
- Follow the WordPress plugin API patterns when possible
- Use TypeScript for type safety and documentation
- Provide backward compatibility for existing implementations
- Design for extensibility

## API Components

- `registerBlockExtension`: Used to extend existing blocks with additional functionality
- `registerIcons`: Used to register custom icons for use in the block editor

## Implementation Guidelines

- Include clear error handling and validation
- Provide meaningful error messages
- Document all parameters and return values
- Consider edge cases and default values
- Use WordPress core utilities when available

## Example Use Cases

```typescript
// Registering icons
import { registerIcons } from '@10up/block-components';

registerIcons({
  myCustomIcon: <svg>...</svg>,
});

// Extending a block
import { registerBlockExtension } from '@10up/block-components';

registerBlockExtension('core/paragraph', {
  extensionName: 'custom-extension',
  attributes: {
    customAttribute: {
      type: 'string',
      default: '',
    },
  },
  edit: (props) => {
    // Custom edit component
  },
});
```

